From 53aa6841c1d6ac613ad84a0c4770bee8ea890139 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ws07 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:34:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] Web client: a record not read is not an empty one; 04's
 open send states kept apart
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Spectator (workstream 08's finding): when the first /h/events page failed,
  FS.chronicle stayed undefined and refreshChronicle threw on
  `FS.chronicle.filter`, so the refresh never finished. A thrown read is now
  a failed read, FS.chronicleRead says how the last poll went, and
  FS.chronicle stays undefined until a page is read.
- screens/chronicle.mjs chronicleState/readLine: loading, not read ("does
  not mean the record is empty"), older (the last poll failed, what was
  read before stays); the spectator's highlights and clashes say "not
  known" instead of "No clash yet" when nothing was read.
- fplay.track: a read that never answers is `unqueryable` (TxUnqueryable),
  apart from GET /f/tx's `unknown`; neither is a failure (04's
  EXECUTION-CONTRACT-20261106 §1). hud/statusview.mjs sendView: 04's seven
  states, each with its own symbol and words.
- Tests (no key, no signature): ws07-spectate unit (fails before the fix
  with the TypeError), ws07-sendstates, and ws07-spectate.screen.mjs in
  English, phone and PC, on the fixture server with /h/events failing in
  the browser.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C5Nj2bNLFpFghsNM9fsQG5
